Trust this connection's own just-committed refs in chunkStoreForceRefresh
(Emscripten only).

- chunkStoreForceRefresh's fast path (csDiskStateMatchesMemory) proves the
  on-disk store matches memory by stat-ing the file and reading its tail root
  record through the chunk store's own long-lived handle
- on native VFSes a write through that handle is immediately visible to a stat
  on the same handle, so the fast path fires right after this connection's own
  commit, and still reliably catches a concurrent peer writer (whose write
  changes the physical file size that stat reports)
- Emscripten's DriveFS (shares a filesystem across worker threads) lacks the
  first property: writes are buffered on the open stream and only pushed to
  the backing store when the stream closes, but stat/getattr is served from
  the backing store regardless of any still-open writer
- so on wasm, the stat-based check reports a same-connection commit as stale
  even though nothing changed, sending chunkStoreForceRefresh down the reload
  path; right after `dolt_clone`, that reload replaces the in-memory refs
  table with a fresh but momentarily still-stale view missing the `origin`
  remote `dolt_clone` itself just added, so the very next statement --
  `dolt_remote('set-url', 'origin', ...)`, run by rusqdoltlite to restore the
  canonical clone URL -- fails with SQLITE_NOTFOUND ("remote not found")

Add a one-shot ChunkStore::bTrustLocalAfterCommit flag, compiled in only
under __EMSCRIPTEN__: chunkStoreCommit sets it after a successful on-disk
commit, and chunkStoreForceRefresh's fast path treats it as equivalent to
csDiskStateMatchesMemory returning true, clearing it either way once
consumed. This is guarded to Emscripten specifically because it trades away
disk-verified peer-write detection for that one call -- safe there because
Emscripten's execution model is synchronous and single-threaded, so nothing
can interleave a conflicting write between this connection's own commit and
its very next statement, but not a trade worth making on native, where the
original disk probe already works correctly and cheaply catches a real
concurrent writer. Native and other non-Emscripten targets compile
byte-for-byte identically to before this patch.

diff --git a/doltlite.c b/doltlite.c
index 81a8e2e..83b9bb5 100644
--- a/doltlite.c
+++ b/doltlite.c
@@ -23646,6 +23646,21 @@ struct ChunkStore {
 
   /* Prevent checkpoint reentry through VFS write hooks. */
   int checkpointActive;
+
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+  /* One-shot flag, Emscripten only:
+  ** - set right after this connection's own chunkStoreCommit persists to disk
+  ** - consumed (cleared) by the very next chunkStoreForceRefresh call
+  ** - DriveFS only makes a written file's stat/size visible after the writing
+  **   stream closes, so csDiskStateMatchesMemory can report a same-connection
+  **   commit as stale even though nothing changed, tripping a spurious reload
+  **   that drops refs a just-run dolt_clone/dolt_remote('set-url') needs
+  ** - safe because Emscripten's execution model is synchronous and
+  **   single-threaded: nothing can interleave a conflicting write in this
+  **   window, unlike native, where this stays off so a real concurrent
+  **   writer is still caught */
+  u8 bTrustLocalAfterCommit;
+#endif
 };
 
 void csManifestSeal(u8 *aBuf);
@@ -97432,6 +97447,21 @@ struct ChunkStore {
 
   /* Prevent checkpoint reentry through VFS write hooks. */
   int checkpointActive;
+
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+  /* One-shot flag, Emscripten only:
+  ** - set right after this connection's own chunkStoreCommit persists to disk
+  ** - consumed (cleared) by the very next chunkStoreForceRefresh call
+  ** - DriveFS only makes a written file's stat/size visible after the writing
+  **   stream closes, so csDiskStateMatchesMemory can report a same-connection
+  **   commit as stale even though nothing changed, tripping a spurious reload
+  **   that drops refs a just-run dolt_clone/dolt_remote('set-url') needs
+  ** - safe because Emscripten's execution model is synchronous and
+  **   single-threaded: nothing can interleave a conflicting write in this
+  **   window, unlike native, where this stays off so a real concurrent
+  **   writer is still caught */
+  u8 bTrustLocalAfterCommit;
+#endif
 };
 
 void csManifestSeal(u8 *aBuf);
@@ -277329,6 +277359,9 @@ int chunkStoreCommit(ChunkStore *cs){
     acquiredLock = 1;
   }
   rc = csCommitToFile(cs);
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+  if( rc==SQLITE_OK ) cs->bTrustLocalAfterCommit = 1;
+#endif
   if( acquiredLock ) chunkStoreUnlock(cs);
   return rc;
 }
@@ -277518,9 +277551,18 @@ int chunkStoreForceRefresh(ChunkStore *cs){
   ** matches this handle's state, the reload — which replays the entire WAL —
   ** is a no-op and can be skipped. Local uncommitted appends fall through so
   ** the reload path keeps reporting SQLITE_BUSY_SNAPSHOT. */
+#if defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+  if( cs->staging.nRecentUncommitted==0
+   && (csDiskStateMatchesMemory(cs) || cs->bTrustLocalAfterCommit) ){
+    cs->bTrustLocalAfterCommit = 0;
+    return SQLITE_OK;
+  }
+  cs->bTrustLocalAfterCommit = 0;
+#else
   if( cs->staging.nRecentUncommitted==0 && csDiskStateMatchesMemory(cs) ){
     return SQLITE_OK;
   }
+#endif
   /* Reload even under a pinned snapshot — the VC write needs the true on-disk
   ** branch tips. Unpin around it (the heuristic refresh path suppresses reloads
   ** while pinned), then restore the pin. */
